# state.log — Example First-Pass Output

This example shows the state.log file from a completed first-pass investigation of a non-EU site. state.log contains ONLY D2:State (single entry at top, replaced at trigger points) and D1 phase summaries (ordered bottom-up, newest above oldest). All typed entries (BUDGET_STATUS, SYSTEM, REQUEST, etc.) live in the gate D0 files — never here.

For EU sites, additional D1 content would include: Pre-Brief `geo_requirements: EU`, P7c consent flow observations in g1d0.log (referenced via D1's `ents:` range).

---

## D2: State
Phase: P13 | Key: SSR, /v2/articles, cursor pagination, no auth, IO lazy loading
Dead ends: shadow DOM ✗, GraphQL ✗ | Open: cursor token type? rate limit?
Budget: 21/60 cycles used | current_d0: g2d0.log
Last checkpoint: P13

## D1: Content Discovery (P9-P13c) | ents: g2:001-g2:009
24 items visible on first load, IntersectionObserver lazy loading detected (g2:002)
IO endpoint: GET /v2/articles?offset=24 (batch size 8, total count signal: none)
Card selector: .article-card (stable), root: main.stream (stable)
Pagination: XHR GET /v2/articles?cursor=abc123 → JSON { items: [...], next_cursor: "...", has_more: true } (g2:003)
Depth probe: pages 2-3 consistent (fast path), cursor pagination stable
Deep web: search form (.search-box) triggers XHR to /v2/search?q=test → returns 15 items (g2:004)
Crawl trap: none detected (cursor-based, not date-based)
BUDGET_STATUS at cycle 21: content_discovery_complete, 39 cycles remaining (g2:006)
First pass complete: 21 cycles used (13 baseline + 8 content) (g2:007, g2:008)

## D1: Baseline (P0-P8a) | ents: g1:001-g1:009
CDP ✓, SSR (Next.js Pages Router), cookies 8 (2 auth: A1S, A3)
Window globals: __NEXT_DATA__ with pageProps → 24 items
Sitemap: 142 URLs, 6 pattern clusters. Deep web: /search?q= (3 URLs)
robots.txt: no specific UA blocks, Crawl-delay: 1
Cookie dependency: Step 1 GET / → [A1, A1S, GUCS, A3] → Step 2 GET /v2/articles requires [A1, A1S] (g1:009)
